STYLE: A grand hand-made toy theatre production built from painted corrugated cardboard. Every piece is a flat cutout of cardboard about 4 mm thick, cut by hand with a craft knife. The front of each piece is painted in opaque matte gouache with bold, simple shapes, large calm areas of colour, visible brush strokes and a few touches of real gold leaf. Few small details: the piece must read from the back row and never look busy. Figures have elegant, slightly long storybook proportions, simple painted faces with dark almond eyes, soft rosy cheeks and a few confident brush lines. Puppet joints are brass split pins. Palette: dusk rose #E9A7A0, amber #E89B4A, dusk blue #2E3A66, pale gold #F2D27A, star white #FFF6DA, rust red #A34A2A, brass #C8963E, reed olive #6E7A4A, stone grey #8C8F99, with raw cardboard brown #A57E52 at cut edges. The mood is tender, sentimental and heroic, like a beloved fairy tale staged with love. A frontier fantasy that belongs to no real culture.
CONSTRAINTS: No text, no lettering, no numbers, no logos, no signature, no watermark. No photographic people, no 3D render look, no plastic, no glossy finish.
REFERENCES: Image 1 is the look reference. Match its paint, gold leaf, palette and figure style. Do not copy its composition. Do not paint a theatre, a stage or curtains.
COMPOSITION: A tall portrait poster for this production, painted in the same gouache and gold-leaf style as Image 1, like a hand-printed poster from a grand old playhouse. One calm, strong composition with a single clear focal point. A slim ornamental painted border frames the picture. Keep a plain, quiet band of warm cream paper across the top fifth of the poster and across the bottom sixth: lettering goes there later, so nothing is painted in those bands. No text anywhere.
SUBJECT: Bayu, a young bugler in plain leather armour and a rust red cloak, as a painted cardboard rod puppet with brass split pins, stands on a rough rock summit and plays his brass bugle toward the sky. Above him rises Kirana, the fallen star, a young woman of pale warm gold light whose long hair streams behind her like the tail of a comet, in a simple gown of dusk blue that fades to gold at the hem. She reaches down toward him as she rises. The sky turns from amber at the horizon to dusk blue at the top, with one bright evening star. Far below, a small stone fort with one round watchtower and warm windows on a hill.
